quotScheme -- Calculates the defining equations for Quot schemes of points
**************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        quotScheme(Q,n,L)
  * Inputs:
      * Q, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, 
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 

Description
===========

The Quot scheme of n points of \mathcal{O}^p on \mathbb{P}^r embeds as a closed
subscheme of the  Grassmannian of rank n quotients  of a push forward of
\mathcal{O}(d)^p. This function gives the defining equations of this closed
subscheme.

+--------------------------+
|i1 : S=ZZ[x_0,x_1];       |
+--------------------------+
|i2 : quotScheme(S^2,1,{0})|
|                          |
|o2 = ideal(a a  - a )     |
|            2 3    4      |
|                          |
|o2 : Ideal of ZZ[a ..a ]  |
|                  1   4   |
+--------------------------+

